IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc24-evidence.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part XXII (Procuring Attendance), sections 709 to 715.2:
-- Evidence on Commission, Video and Audio Evidence, Evidence Previously Taken, Video-recorded Evidence.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), part agent ccc24. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How to read an answer: see the header of ccc24-appeal-procedure.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING; a caller must never turn NOTHING into JUST FALSE).
-- A function named "may" whose "if" or "who" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12); one whose "where"/"when"/"on" gate fails answers JUST FALSE and is listed (ruling (b)).
-- A function that is not named "may" (for example "is admissible") answers JUST FALSE where a condition the text introduces with "if" or "unless" fails.

§ `Part XXII -- Evidence on Commission (sections 709 to 714)`

§§ `Sections 709 to 713.1 -- Evidence on commission`

-- 709(1): the party's liberty to apply; the witness limbs are (a) "not likely to be able to attend at the time the trial is held" (illness or other good and sufficient cause) or (b) "out of Canada".
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14670 | 709 (1) A party to proceedings by way of indictment or summary conviction may apply for an order appointing a commissioner to take the evidence of a witness who
-- src:14671 | (a) is, by reason of
-- src:14672 | (i) physical disability arising out of illness, or
-- src:14673 | (ii) any other good and sufficient cause,
-- src:14674 | not likely to be able to attend at the time the trial is held; or
-- src:14675 | (b) is out of Canada.
@ref s 709(1) (src:14670-14675)
GIVEN `the person is a party to proceedings by way of indictment or summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness is, by reason of physical disability arising out of illness or any other good and sufficient cause, not likely to be able to attend at the time the trial is held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness is out of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 709(1) the party may apply for an order appointing a commissioner to take the evidence of the witness` MEANS
    IF `the person is a party to proceedings by way of indictment or summary conviction` AND (`the witness is, by reason of physical disability arising out of illness or any other good and sufficient cause, not likely to be able to attend at the time the trial is held` OR `the witness is out of Canada`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to take the evidence of a witness who"

-- src:14677 | (2) A decision under subsection (1) is deemed to have been made at the trial held in relation to the proceedings mentioned in that subsection.
@ref s 709(2) (src:14677-14677)
GIVEN `the decision is a decision under subsection 709(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 709(2) the decision is deemed to have been made at the trial held in relation to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a decision under subsection 709(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A decision under subsection (1) is deemed to have been made at the trial held in relation to the proceedings mentioned in that subsection"

DECLARE `s 710(1) forum` IS ONE OF
    `s 710(1)(a) a judge of a superior court of the province in which the proceedings are taken`
    `s 710(1)(b) a judge of a county or district court in the territorial division in which the proceedings are taken`
    `s 710(1)(c) a provincial court judge`
    `s 710(1) another forum`

-- 710(1)(c) "where (i) the accused is before a provincial court judge presiding over a preliminary inquiry ... or (ii) the accused or defendant is to be tried by a provincial court judge": a where-gate.
-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14679 | 710 (1) An application under paragraph 709(1)(a) shall be made
-- src:14680 | (a) to a judge of a superior court of the province in which the proceedings are taken;
-- src:14681 | (b) to a judge of a county or district court in the territorial division in which the proceedings are taken; or
-- src:14682 | (c) to a provincial court judge, where
-- src:14683 | (i) at the time the application is made, the accused is before a provincial court judge presiding over a preliminary inquiry under Part XVIII, or
-- src:14684 | (ii) the accused or defendant is to be tried by a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or XXVII.
@ref s 710(1) (src:14679-14684)
GIVEN forum IS A `s 710(1) forum`
      `the application is an application under paragraph 709(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the application is made the accused is before a provincial court judge presiding over a preliminary inquiry under Part XVIII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused or defendant is to be tried by a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or XXVII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 710(1) the application shall be made to the forum` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is an application under paragraph 709(1)(a)`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application under paragraph 709(1)(a) shall be made"
        IF forum EQUALS `s 710(1) another forum`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "shall be made (a) to a judge of a superior court of the province"
        IF forum EQUALS `s 710(1)(c) a provincial court judge` AND (NOT (`at the time the application is made the accused is before a provincial court judge presiding over a preliminary inquiry under Part XVIII` OR `the accused or defendant is to be tried by a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or XXVII`))
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to a provincial court judge, where"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14686 | (2) An application under subparagraph 709(1)(a)(i) may be granted on the evidence of a registered medical practitioner.
@ref s 710(2) (src:14686-14686)
GIVEN `the application is an application under subparagraph 709(1)(a)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is the evidence of a registered medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 710(2) the application may be granted on the evidence of a registered medical practitioner` MEANS
    IF `the application is an application under subparagraph 709(1)(a)(i)` AND `the evidence is the evidence of a registered medical practitioner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application under subparagraph 709(1)(a)(i) may be granted on the evidence of a registered medical practitioner"

-- 711: "Where the evidence of a witness mentioned in paragraph 709(1)(a) is taken by a commissioner appointed under section 710" is a where-gate (JUST FALSE); "it may be admitted ... if (a), (b) and (c)" an if-gate (NOTHING).
-- @tag grant=flip
-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14688 | 711 Where the evidence of a witness mentioned in paragraph 709(1)(a) is taken by a commissioner appointed under section 710, it may be admitted in evidence in the proceedings if
-- src:14689 | (a) it is proved by oral evidence or by affidavit that the witness is unable to attend by reason of death or physical disability arising out of illness or some other good and sufficient cause;
-- src:14690 | (b) the transcript of the evidence is signed by the commissioner by or before whom it purports to have been taken; and
-- src:14691 | (c) it is proved to the satisfaction of the court that reasonable notice of the time for taking the evidence was given to the other party, and that the accused or his counsel, or the prosecutor or his counsel, as the case may be, had or might have had full opportunity to cross-examine the witness.
@ref s 711 (src:14688-14691)
GIVEN `the evidence of a witness mentioned in paragraph 709(1)(a) is taken by a commissioner appointed under section 710` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved by oral evidence or by affidavit that the witness is unable to attend by reason of death or physical disability arising out of illness or some other good and sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transcript of the evidence is signed by the commissioner by or before whom it purports to have been taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved to the satisfaction of the court that reasonable notice of the time for taking the evidence was given to the other party and that the accused or counsel, or the prosecutor or counsel, as the case may be, had or might have had full opportunity to cross-examine the witness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 711 the evidence may be admitted in evidence in the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the evidence of a witness mentioned in paragraph 709(1)(a) is taken by a commissioner appointed under section 710`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the evidence of a witness mentioned in paragraph 709(1)(a) is taken by a commissioner appointed under section 710"
        IF    `it is proved by oral evidence or by affidavit that the witness is unable to attend by reason of death or physical disability arising out of illness or some other good and sufficient cause`
          AND `the transcript of the evidence is signed by the commissioner by or before whom it purports to have been taken`
          AND `it is proved to the satisfaction of the court that reasonable notice of the time for taking the evidence was given to the other party and that the accused or counsel, or the prosecutor or counsel, as the case may be, had or might have had full opportunity to cross-examine the witness`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it may be admitted in evidence in the proceedings if"

DECLARE `s 712(1) forum` IS ONE OF
    `s 712(1)(a) a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or of a court of criminal jurisdiction before which the accused is to be tried`
    `s 712(1)(b) a provincial court judge`
    `s 712(1) another forum`

