      `the accused or defendant is to be tried by a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or XXVII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 712(1) the application shall be made to the forum` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is an application under paragraph 709(1)(b)`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application that is made under paragraph 709(1)(b) shall be made"
        IF forum EQUALS `s 712(1) another forum`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "shall be made (a) to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction"
        IF forum EQUALS `s 712(1)(b) a provincial court judge` AND (NOT `the accused or defendant is to be tried by a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or XXVII`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to a provincial court judge, where the accused or defendant is to be tried by a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or XXVII"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- @tag grant=where
