      `the evidence has otherwise been taken in accordance with the order and with Part XXII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 713(1) the failure of the accused to be present or represented prevents the admission of the evidence in the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the accused failed to be present or to be represented by counsel in accordance with the order` AND `the evidence has otherwise been taken in accordance with the order and with Part XXII`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not prevent the admission of the evidence in the proceedings if the evidence has otherwise been taken in accordance with the order and with this Part"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "failure of the accused to be present or to be represented by counsel in accordance with the order"

