-- 713.1: "shall not be excluded by reason only that it would have been taken differently in Canada, provided that ...": JUST FALSE (not excluded on that ground alone) where the proviso is met.
-- src:14704 | 713.1 Evidence taken by a commissioner appointed under section 712 shall not be excluded by reason only that it would have been taken differently in Canada, provided that the process used to take the evidence is consistent with the law of the country where it was taken and that the process used to take the evidence was not contrary to the principles of fundamental justice.
@ref s 713.1 (src:14704-14704)
GIVEN `the evidence was taken by a commissioner appointed under section 712` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence would have been taken differently in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process used to take the evidence is consistent with the law of the country where it was taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process used to take the evidence was not contrary to the principles of fundamental justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 713.1 the evidence is excluded by reason only that it would have been taken differently in Canada` MEANS
    IF    `the evidence was taken by a commissioner appointed under section 712`
      AND `the evidence would have been taken differently in Canada`
      AND `the process used to take the evidence is consistent with the law of the country where it was taken`
      AND `the process used to take the evidence was not contrary to the principles of fundamental justice`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be excluded by reason only that it would have been taken differently in Canada, provided that the process used to take the evidence is consistent with the law of the country where it was taken"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "provided that the process used to take the evidence is consistent with the law of the country where it was taken"

-- src:14706 | 714 Except where otherwise provided by this Part or by rules of court, the practice and procedure in connection with the appointment of commissioners under this Part, the taking of evidence by commissioners, the certifying and return thereof and the use of the evidence in the proceedings shall, as far as possible, be the same as those that govern like matters in civil proceedings in the superior court of the province in which the proceedings are taken.
