    BRANCH
        IF `this Part or rules of court otherwise provide`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except where otherwise provided by this Part or by rules of court"
        IF `the matter is the appointment of commissioners, the taking of evidence by commissioners, the certifying and return of the evidence or the use of the evidence in the proceedings`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the practice and procedure in connection with the appointment of commissioners under this Part, the taking of evidence by commissioners"

§ `Part XXII -- Video and Audio Evidence (sections 714.1 to 714.8)`

§§ `Sections 714.1 to 714.8`

DECLARE `s 714.1 circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 714.1(a) the location and personal circumstances of the witness`
    `s 714.1(b) the costs that would be incurred if the witness were to appear in person`
    `s 714.1(c) the nature of the witness anticipated evidence`
    `s 714.1(d) the suitability of the location from where the witness will give evidence`
    `s 714.1(e) the accused's right to a fair and public hearing`
    `s 714.1(f) the nature and seriousness of the offence`
    `s 714.1(g) any potential prejudice to the parties caused by the fact that the witness would not be seen by them, if the court were to order the evidence to be given by audioconference`
    `s 714.1 another circumstance`

-- 714.1(a) to (g): the court's opinion is "having regard to all the circumstances, including" these: every circumstance is to be regarded, so the answer is JUST TRUE for each.
-- src:14711 | (a) the location and personal circumstances of the witness;
-- src:14712 | (b) the costs that would be incurred if the witness were to appear in person;
-- src:14713 | (c) the nature of the witness’ anticipated evidence;
-- src:14714 | (d) the suitability of the location from where the witness will give evidence;
-- src:14715 | (e) the accused’s right to a fair and public hearing;
-- src:14716 | (f) the nature and seriousness of the offence; and
-- src:14717 | (g) any potential prejudice to the parties caused by the fact that the witness would not be seen by them, if the court were to order the evidence to be given by audioconference.
@ref s 714.1(a) to (g) (src:14711-14717)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 714.1 circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714.1 the court is to have regard to the circumstance in forming its opinion` MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `s 714.1 another circumstance` THEN JUST TRUE   -- the text says "all the circumstances, including": a circumstance not listed is also to be regarded
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 714.1: "if the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances": the opinion is a plain input.
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14710 | 714.1 A court may order that a witness in Canada give evidence by audioconference or videoconference, if the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances, including
@ref s 714.1 (src:14710-14710)
GIVEN `the witness is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714.1 the court may order that the witness give evidence by audioconference or videoconference` MEANS
    IF `the witness is in Canada` AND `the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances"

-- src:14719 | 714.2 (1) A court shall receive evidence given by a witness outside Canada by videoconference, unless one of the parties satisfies the court that the reception of such testimony would be contrary to the principles of fundamental justice.
@ref s 714.2(1) (src:14719-14719)
GIVEN `the witness is outside Canada and gives evidence by videoconference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the parties satisfies the court that the reception of such testimony would be contrary to the principles of fundamental justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714.2(1) the court shall receive the evidence given by the witness by videoconference` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the witness is outside Canada and gives evidence by videoconference`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "evidence given by a witness outside Canada by videoconference"
        IF `one of the parties satisfies the court that the reception of such testimony would be contrary to the principles of fundamental justice`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless one of the parties satisfies the court that the reception of such testimony would be contrary to the principles of fundamental justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 714.2(2): "not less than 10 days before the witness is scheduled to testify": a fixed period, so a notice with fewer than ten days answers JUST FALSE.
-- src:14721 | (2) A party who wishes to call a witness to give evidence under subsection (1) shall give notice to the court before which the evidence is to be given and the other parties of their intention to do so not less than 10 days before the witness is scheduled to testify.
@ref s 714.2(2) (src:14721-14721)
GIVEN `the party wishes to call a witness to give evidence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has given notice to the court and the other parties of their intention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days before the witness is scheduled to testify at which the notice was given or would be given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714.2(2) the party gave the notice in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the party wishes to call a witness to give evidence under subsection (1)`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A party who wishes to call a witness to give evidence under subsection (1)"
        IF `the number of days before the witness is scheduled to testify at which the notice was given or would be given` LESS THAN 10
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not less than 10 days before the witness is scheduled to testify"
        IF `the party has given notice to the court and the other parties of their intention`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall give notice to the court before which the evidence is to be given and the other parties of their intention"

