        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that is given by a witness who is outside of Canada"
        IF manner EQUALS `s 714.5 another manner`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "shall be given (a) under oath or affirmation in accordance with Canadian law"
        IF manner EQUALS `s 714.5(c) in any other manner that demonstrates that the witness understands that they must tell the truth` AND (NOT `the manner demonstrates that the witness understands that they must tell the truth`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any other manner that demonstrates that the witness understands that they must tell the truth"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:14734 | 714.6 When a witness who is outside Canada gives evidence under section 714.2 or 714.3, the evidence is deemed to be given in Canada, and given under oath or affirmation in accordance with Canadian law, for the purposes of the laws relating to evidence, procedure, perjury and contempt of court.
@ref s 714.6 (src:14734-14734)
GIVEN `the witness is outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness gives evidence under section 714.2 or 714.3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714.6 the evidence is deemed to be given in Canada, and given under oath or affirmation in accordance with Canadian law, for the purposes of the laws relating to evidence, procedure, perjury and contempt of court` MEANS
    IF `the witness is outside Canada` AND `the witness gives evidence under section 714.2 or 714.3`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "When a witness who is outside Canada gives evidence under section 714.2 or 714.3"

-- src:14736 | 714.7 Unless the court orders otherwise, a party who calls a witness to give evidence by means of the technology referred to in section 714.1, 714.2 or 714.3 shall pay any costs associated with the use of the technology.
@ref s 714.7 (src:14736-14736)
GIVEN `the party calls a witness to give evidence by means of the technology referred to in section 714.1, 714.2 or 714.3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714.7 the party shall pay the costs associated with the use of the technology` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the party calls a witness to give evidence by means of the technology referred to in section 714.1, 714.2 or 714.3`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a party who calls a witness to give evidence by means of the technology"
        IF `the court orders otherwise`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the court orders otherwise"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:14738 | 714.8 Nothing in sections 714.1 to 714.7 is to be construed as preventing a court from receiving evidence by audioconference or videoconference, if the parties so consent.
@ref s 714.8 (src:14738-14738)
GIVEN `the parties consent to the court receiving evidence by audioconference or videoconference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714.8 sections 714.1 to 714.7 prevent the court from receiving evidence by audioconference or videoconference` MEANS
    IF `the parties consent to the court receiving evidence by audioconference or videoconference`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in sections 714.1 to 714.7 is to be construed as preventing a court from receiving evidence by audioconference or videoconference, if the parties so consent"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "if the parties so consent"

§ `Part XXII -- Evidence Previously Taken (sections 715 to 715.01)`

§§ `Section 715 -- Evidence at preliminary inquiry may be read at trial in certain cases`

-- 715(1): "may be admitted as evidence in the proceedings without further proof, unless the accused proves that the accused did not have full opportunity to cross-examine".
-- The two "where" gates (the earlier evidence and its trigger; proof of the accused's presence) answer JUST FALSE where they fail (ruling (b)); the "unless" is a closing exception.
-- @tag grant=where
-- @tag grant=closed
-- src:14742 | 715 (1) Where, at the trial of an accused, a person whose evidence was given at a previous trial on the same charge, or whose evidence was taken in the investigation of the charge against the accused or on the preliminary inquiry into the charge, refuses to be sworn or to give evidence, or if facts are proved on oath from which it can be inferred reasonably that the person
-- src:14743 | (a) is dead,
-- src:14744 | (b) has since become and is insane,
-- src:14745 | (c) is so ill that he is unable to travel or testify, or
-- src:14746 | (d) is absent from Canada,
-- src:14747 | and where it is proved that the evidence was taken in the presence of the accused, it may be admitted as evidence in the proceedings without further proof, unless the accused proves that the accused did not have full opportunity to cross-examine the witness.
@ref s 715(1) (src:14742-14747)
GIVEN `at the trial of an accused, a person gave evidence at a previous trial on the same charge, or evidence of the person was taken in the investigation of the charge or on the preliminary inquiry into the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person refuses to be sworn or to give evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `facts are proved on oath from which it can be inferred reasonably that the person is dead, has since become and is insane, is so ill that the person is unable to travel or testify, or is absent from Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the evidence was taken in the presence of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused proves that the accused did not have full opportunity to cross-examine the witness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715(1) the evidence may be admitted as evidence in the proceedings without further proof` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`at the trial of an accused, a person gave evidence at a previous trial on the same charge, or evidence of the person was taken in the investigation of the charge or on the preliminary inquiry into the charge` AND (`the person refuses to be sworn or to give evidence` OR `facts are proved on oath from which it can be inferred reasonably that the person is dead, has since become and is insane, is so ill that the person is unable to travel or testify, or is absent from Canada`))
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, at the trial of an accused, a person whose evidence was given at a previous trial on the same charge"
        IF NOT `it is proved that the evidence was taken in the presence of the accused`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and where it is proved that the evidence was taken in the presence of the accused"
        IF `the accused proves that the accused did not have full opportunity to cross-examine the witness`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the accused proves that the accused did not have full opportunity to cross-examine the witness"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14749 | (2) Evidence that has been taken on the preliminary inquiry or other investigation of a charge against an accused may be admitted as evidence in the prosecution of the accused for any other offence on the same proof and in the same manner in all respects, as it might, according to law, be admitted as evidence in the prosecution of the offence with which the accused was charged when the evidence was taken.
@ref s 715(2) (src:14749-14749)
GIVEN `the evidence has been taken on the preliminary inquiry or other investigation of a charge against an accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecution is a prosecution of the accused for any other offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is admitted on the same proof and in the same manner in all respects as it might, according to law, be admitted in the prosecution of the offence with which the accused was charged when the evidence was taken` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715(2) the evidence may be admitted as evidence in the prosecution of the accused for any other offence` MEANS
    IF `the evidence has been taken on the preliminary inquiry or other investigation of a charge against an accused` AND `the prosecution is a prosecution of the accused for any other offence` AND `the evidence is admitted on the same proof and in the same manner in all respects as it might, according to law, be admitted in the prosecution of the offence with which the accused was charged when the evidence was taken`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the same proof and in the same manner in all respects, as it might, according to law, be admitted as evidence in the prosecution of the offence with which the accused was charged"

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14751 | (2.1) Despite subsections (1) and (2), evidence that has been taken at a preliminary inquiry in the absence of the accused may be admitted as evidence for the purposes referred to in those subsections if the accused was absent further to the permission of a justice granted under paragraph 537(1)(j.1).
@ref s 715(2.1) (src:14751-14751)
GIVEN `the evidence has been taken at a preliminary inquiry in the absence of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was absent further to the permission of a justice granted under paragraph 537(1)(j.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715(2.1) the evidence taken at a preliminary inquiry in the absence of the accused may be admitted as evidence for the purposes referred to in subsections (1) and (2)` MEANS
    IF `the evidence has been taken at a preliminary inquiry in the absence of the accused` AND `the accused was absent further to the permission of a justice granted under paragraph 537(1)(j.1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "evidence that has been taken at a preliminary inquiry in the absence of the accused may be admitted as evidence for the purposes referred to in those subsections if the accused was absent further to the permission of a justice granted under paragraph 537(1)(j.1)"

-- src:14753 | (3) For the purposes of this section, where evidence was taken at a previous trial or preliminary hearing or other proceeding in respect of an accused in the absence of the accused, who was absent by reason of having absconded, the accused is deemed to have been present during the taking of the evidence and to have had full opportunity to cross-examine the witness.
@ref s 715(3) (src:14753-14753)
GIVEN `the evidence was taken at a previous trial or preliminary hearing or other proceeding in respect of the accused in the absence of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was absent by reason of having absconded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715(3) the accused is deemed to have been present during the taking of the evidence and to have had full opportunity to cross-examine the witness` MEANS
    IF `the evidence was taken at a previous trial or preliminary hearing or other proceeding in respect of the accused in the absence of the accused` AND `the accused was absent by reason of having absconded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where evidence was taken at a previous trial or preliminary hearing or other proceeding in respect of an accused in the absence of the accused, who was absent by reason of having absconded"

-- 715(4): "do not apply" is a flat negative: JUST FALSE where the evidence was received under subsection 540(7); the text says nothing else.
-- src:14755 | (4) Subsections (1) to (3) do not apply in respect of evidence received under subsection 540(7).
@ref s 715(4) (src:14755-14755)
GIVEN `the evidence was received under subsection 540(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715(4) subsections 715(1) to (3) apply to the evidence` MEANS
    IF `the evidence was received under subsection 540(7)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) to (3) do not apply in respect of evidence received under subsection 540(7)"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Subsections (1) to (3) do not apply in respect of evidence received under subsection 540(7)"

§§ `Section 715.01 -- Transcript of evidence`

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14757 | 715.01 (1) Despite section 715, the transcript of testimony given by a police officer, as defined in section 183, in the presence of an accused during a voir dire or preliminary inquiry held in relation to the accused’s trial may be received in evidence at that trial.
@ref s 715.01(1) (src:14757-14757)
GIVEN `the testimony was given by a police officer, as defined in section 183` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testimony was given in the presence of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testimony was given during a voir dire or preliminary inquiry held in relation to the accused's trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.01(1) the transcript of testimony given by a police officer in the presence of the accused during a voir dire or preliminary inquiry may be received in evidence at the trial` MEANS
    IF `the testimony was given by a police officer, as defined in section 183` AND `the testimony was given in the presence of the accused` AND `the testimony was given during a voir dire or preliminary inquiry held in relation to the accused's trial`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the transcript of testimony given by a police officer, as defined in section 183, in the presence of an accused during a voir dire or preliminary inquiry held in relation to the accused’s trial may be received in evidence at that trial"

-- src:14759 | (2) No transcript is to be received in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has given to the party against whom it is intended to be produced reasonable notice of that intention together with a copy of the transcript.
@ref s 715.01(2) (src:14759-14759)
GIVEN `the transcript is a transcript referred to in subsection 715.01(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party intending to produce the transcript has given to the party against whom it is intended to be produced reasonable notice of that intention together with a copy of the transcript` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.01(2) the bar on receiving the transcript in evidence applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the transcript is a transcript referred to in subsection 715.01(1)`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No transcript is to be received in evidence"
        IF `the party intending to produce the transcript has given to the party against whom it is intended to be produced reasonable notice of that intention together with a copy of the transcript`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the party intending to produce it has given to the party against whom it is intended to be produced reasonable notice of that intention together with a copy of the transcript"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- @tag grant=flip
