§ `Part XXII -- Video-recorded Evidence (sections 715.1 and 715.2)`

§§ `Sections 715.1 and 715.2`

-- 715.1(1): not named "may", so an "if" that fails answers JUST FALSE; "unless the presiding judge or justice is of the opinion ..." closes it.
-- src:14771 | 715.1 (1) In any proceeding against an accused in which a victim or other witness was under the age of eighteen years at the time the offence is alleged to have been committed, a video recording made within a reasonable time after the alleged offence, in which the victim or witness describes the acts complained of, is admissible in evidence if the victim or witness, while testifying, adopts the contents of the video recording, unless the presiding judge or justice is of the opinion that admission of the video recording in evidence would interfere with the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 715.1(1) (src:14771-14771)
GIVEN `the proceeding is against an accused and a victim or other witness was under the age of eighteen years at the time the offence is alleged to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the video recording was made within a reasonable time after the alleged offence and the victim or witness describes the acts complained of in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim or witness, while testifying, adopts the contents of the video recording` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the presiding judge or justice is of the opinion that admission of the video recording in evidence would interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.1(1) the video recording is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the proceeding is against an accused and a victim or other witness was under the age of eighteen years at the time the offence is alleged to have been committed` AND `the video recording was made within a reasonable time after the alleged offence and the victim or witness describes the acts complained of in it`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a victim or other witness was under the age of eighteen years at the time the offence is alleged to have been committed"
        IF `the presiding judge or justice is of the opinion that admission of the video recording in evidence would interfere with the proper administration of justice`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the presiding judge or justice is of the opinion that admission of the video recording in evidence would interfere with the proper administration of justice"
        IF NOT `the victim or witness, while testifying, adopts the contents of the video recording`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is admissible in evidence if the victim or witness, while testifying, adopts the contents of the video recording"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14773 | (2) The presiding judge or justice may prohibit any other use of a video recording referred to in subsection (1).
@ref s 715.1(2) (src:14773-14773)
GIVEN `the video recording is a video recording referred to in subsection 715.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is a use other than its admission in evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.1(2) the presiding judge or justice may prohibit any other use of the video recording` MEANS
    IF `the video recording is a video recording referred to in subsection 715.1(1)` AND `the use is a use other than its admission in evidence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The presiding judge or justice may prohibit any other use of a video recording referred to in subsection (1)"

-- src:14775 | 715.2 (1) In any proceeding against an accused in which a victim or other witness is able to communicate evidence but may have difficulty doing so by reason of a mental or physical disability, a video recording made within a reasonable time after the alleged offence, in which the victim or witness describes the acts complained of, is admissible in evidence if the victim or witness, while testifying, adopts the contents of the video recording, unless the presiding judge or justice is of the opinion that admission of the video recording in evidence would interfere with the proper administration of justice.
